From 315e9277099a242a65605268e9544efdcd9b7ce5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 08:17:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Deleted Accounts page for Super Admin (item 14,
 complete)

New page showing every deleted user and deleted dealer, in separate
tabs since they're different collections with different fields.
Reuses the existing DELETE /admin/users/{userId}?cascade=true
endpoint for the actual wipe - already handles every role correctly
(for a DEALER_ADMIN, also removes their dealer org, every car
listed, staff accounts, expenses, and sales), no new backend
endpoint needed for it.

Wipe requires two separate confirmations before anything happens:
a danger-styled confirm dialog explaining exactly what gets removed,
then typing WIPE as an explicit second step - this is genuinely
irreversible, so it shouldn't be reachable by a single misclick.

Every wipe is a deliberate, individually-confirmed Super Admin
decision - nothing here runs automatically or on a timer, matching
exactly what was asked: history stays visible until Super Admin
decides (at the account owner's request or their own judgment) to
permanently remove it.

Added to the Super Admin sidebar and the global search registry so
it's actually discoverable, not just reachable by typing the URL.
